.el .ds Aq '
.TH FATHOM_COMPLETIONS_MAN 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-completions\-man \- The man pages, rendered from the same grammar
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom completions man\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR] [\fB\-\-page\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
The man pages, rendered from the same grammar
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Write them under `DIR` (as `DIR/man1/*.1`) instead of printing one page on stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-page\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Just this page — `\-\-page fathom\-check` — instead of every verb
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
